cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "CompProGraph: Lossless Graph Compression for W3C PROV-JSON Corpora"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-06-12"
url: "https://github.com/nickjones39/CompProGraph"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  CompProGraph is a lossless, single-pass compression framework for W3C PROV-JSON
  provenance graph corpora. It combines structural signature hashing (supernode
  templates with columnar edge encoding) and corpus-wide dictionary encoding to
  achieve ~72.5% storage reduction while guaranteeing exact canonical-JSON
  round-trip reconstruction. Evaluated on the OpenML-CC18 benchmark corpus as
  part of research into provenance-based cybersecurity for LLMs.
